	(text "MCU: STM32G0B1CBT6 (LQFP48), USB device, SPI to the isolated stage, SPI to the display"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18.0 22.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 4.5 4.5)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 40 90 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1661b21b-dc9c-51ed-aa16-727d9cc18f1e")
	)
	(text "Crystal-less: USB SOF trims the 48 MHz HSI. DFU over USB is in ROM (hold BOOT, tap RESET). Everything here is on DGND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18.0 26.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(italic yes)
				(color 70 70 70 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f69940a6-87ee-5659-9cff-855eedc1cc8f")
	)
	(text "Pin plan (STM32G0B1CBT6, LQFP48)\nSPI1   PA5 SCK, PA6 MISO, PA7 MOSI, PA4 /CS DAC, PB0 /CS ADC, PB1 LOAD_OFF (isolator)\nSPI2   PB13 SCK, PB15 MOSI, PB12 /CS = MAX7219 LOAD (display chain, via 74AHCT125)\nTIM3   PB4 / PB5 encoder, PB3 push.  TIM17 PB9 fan PWM, TIM16 PB8 tach, PD3 FAN_EN\nADC    PA0 / PA1 = CC1 / CC2.  USB PA11 DM, PA12 DP, crystal-less (CRS)\nUSART1 PA9 / PA10 debug.  I2C1 PB6 / PB7 OLED.  PD0 ON/OFF, PD1 MODE, PD2 MENU, PC6 LED\nWhy not the STM32F103RBT6 of Rev B: no USB DFU in its ROM (USART only), needs a\ncrystal, no CRS, same LQFP64 size. The G0B1 is cheaper, smaller, and its ROM DFU\nremoves the second USB port.\nSpare: PA2, PA3, PA8, PA15, PB2, PB10, PB11, PB14, PC7, PC13-PC15, PF0, PF1 (NC)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 31.49 236.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(color 40 40 40 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "761c8b95-4a83-56a2-8708-db86ccd0c642")
	)
	(text "A   Microcontroller"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.4 54.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 50 120 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ac968910-43f5-570f-93ae-a4873707f11a")
	)
	(text "All X7R. One 100 nF per VDD pin, 1 uF + 100 nF at VREF+ (C17, C18).\nPlace within 2 mm of the pins."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 251.49 80.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(color 40 40 40 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1cb03994-9780-586c-b65c-379b1de660c6")
	)
	(text "B   Decoupling"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 247.11 42.97 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 50 120 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "60e5f6cc-e99f-5bf6-a247-7bfd6566eb19")
	)
	(text "BOOT0 shares PA14 (SWCLK) on the STM32G0. Hold BOOT, tap RESET: the ROM bootloader\nenumerates as USB DFU. Once, with STM32CubeProgrammer, clear option bit nBOOT_SEL so\nthe pin is honoured (the factory default ignores it)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 251.49 154.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(color 40 40 40 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d980c992-b841-5d1f-b085-1d324cac6db3")
	)
	(text "C   Reset, BOOT0 (DFU), SWD"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 240.76 92.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 50 120 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5677dc7d-dc72-55b2-b9b8-c5223a9a57d9")
	)
	(text "J5 takes a 0.96\" SSD1306 module for menus and battery statistics;\nthe 7-segment panel is the primary UI."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 251.49 240.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(color 40 40 40 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3777cc82-9238-513c-99d9-add98d25ec0e")
	)
	(text "D   Debug UART, I2C expansion (OLED), status LED"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 242.03 171.24 0)
		(effects
